\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For independent proper uniformly signed random 3-clauses, is there a limiting sharp density $\alpha _3$ and one deterministic finite Turing machine that, on every unary precision input $1^r$, halts with a rational $q_r$ satisfying $|q_r-\alpha _3|\leq 2^{-r}$, using no oracle, advice or noncomputable parameter?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For independent proper uniformly signed random 3-clauses, is there a limiting sharp density $\alpha _3$ and one deterministic finite Turing machine that, on every unary precision input $1^r$, halts with a rational $q_r$ satisfying $|q_r-\alpha _3|\leq 2^{-r}$, using no oracle, advice or noncomputable parameter?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Computing-the-Random-3-SAT-Threshold-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex}.
